# Wave 6, editor-annotations. The command registry gains the annotation verbs,
# and Delete is corrected to what D3 actually says.

file: "packages/editor/src/gestures/commands.ts"
doc: "The one command registry every dispatcher — keymap, toolbar, context menu, palette — runs through."

structs: [
  { name: "CommandContext"
    change_type: MODIFIED
    doc:
      "Gains `beginTextEdit`, called by the commands that create or open an\n"
      "annotation for editing.\n"
      "\n"
      "It is a callback rather than a direct UiState write because the canvas\n"
      "must scroll the annotation into view and focus the editor, neither of\n"
      "which a command can do. The command decides WHAT is being edited; the\n"
      "canvas decides how the editor appears.\n"
      "\n"
      "`beginTextEdit` specifically is REQUIRED, not optional. An optional\n"
      "callback is a promise that something upstream populates it, and nothing\n"
      "checks that anything does -- which is how `focusInspector` shipped as a\n"
      "chord that resolved, dispatched, called undefined and did nothing.\n"
      "\n"
      "This is a rule about NEW callback fields, not a retroactive one.\n"
      "`focusInspector` and `geometry` stay optional and are not changed by\n"
      "this pillar: `geometry` is legitimately absent before the first scene\n"
      "resolves, and re-shaping `focusInspector` is the inspector's business.\n"
      "\n"
      "Two places construct a CommandContext: canvas.tsx, which this pillar\n"
      "changes, and the spyContext in\n"
      "gestures/command_wiring.test.ts, which exists precisely to catch the\n"
      "dead-wire bug described above and deliberately leaves no field unset.\n"
      "Making this field required is a compile error there until it is added,\n"
      "which is the intended effect -- that test is what proves each new\n"
      "command has an observable effect."
    fields: [
      { name: "state",          type: { named: { symbol: "EditorState" } } },
      { name: "ui",             type: { named: { symbol: "UiState" } } },
      { name: "geometry",       type: { named: { symbol: "SceneGeometry" } }, is_optional: true },
      { name: "rect",           type: { named: { symbol: "ContainerRect" } } },
      { name: "save",           type: { unsupported: { reason: RAW_EXPRESSION, source_excerpt: "() => void" } } },
      { name: "focusInspector", type: { unsupported: { reason: RAW_EXPRESSION, source_excerpt: "() => void" } }, is_optional: true },
      { name: "beginTextEdit",  type: { unsupported: { reason: RAW_EXPRESSION, source_excerpt: "(ref: ElementRef) => void" } } }
    ]
  }
]

constants: [
  { name: "COMMANDS"
    change_type: MODIFIED
    doc:
      "Six commands added, and one existing command corrected.\n"
      "\n"
      "'tool-select' and 'tool-annotation' set ui.tool. Nothing else --\n"
      "switching tool must not clear the selection, because picking the\n"
      "annotation tool to annotate the thing you just selected is the common\n"
      "case.\n"
      "\n"
      "'hide' hides every selected node, which is what Delete used to do. D3\n"
      "forbids binding it to Delete; no OTHER chord is assigned either,\n"
      "because its intended surfaces are the context menu and the palette and\n"
      "both are editor-shell's. So it is in this registry, in CommandId, and\n"
      "in no KEYMAP row.\n"
      "\n"
      "'add-annotation' creates one and calls beginTextEdit on it. Its\n"
      "position -- the annotation's TOP-LEFT, which is what AnnotationLayout\n"
      "carries -- is (selectionBounds.maxX + 24, selectionBounds.minY) when\n"
      "something is selected and its bounds are known, so the note sits beside\n"
      "what it is about rather than on top of it.\n"
      "\n"
      "Otherwise the top-left that centres a NEW_ANNOTATION_SIZE box in the\n"
      "visible viewport. 'Otherwise' is BOTH the nothing-selected case and the\n"
      "case where `geometry` is absent, which it may be since the field is\n"
      "optional -- the command must still create an annotation, not silently\n"
      "do nothing.\n"
      "\n"
      "Viewport comes from `rect` and the ui viewport, never from window\n"
      "dimensions: using screen pixels for a canvas position is the §2.11 bug\n"
      "verbatim. Its id comes from newAnnotationId and its text from\n"
      "NEW_ANNOTATION_TEXT, so the resulting edit is replayable.\n"
      "\n"
      "'edit-text' calls beginTextEdit when the selection is exactly one\n"
      "annotation, and does nothing otherwise. Enter is bound to it\n"
      "unconditionally, so 'otherwise' includes every other selection and the\n"
      "empty one.\n"
      "\n"
      "'duplicate' runs duplicateAnnotationEdit once per selected annotation,\n"
      "applying each edit before building the next so that every call sees\n"
      "the ids the previous one wrote -- duplicating two annotations at once\n"
      "must not produce the same id twice. It leaves the COPIES selected,\n"
      "which is what makes duplicate-then-drag work. Non-annotation selections are skipped -- duplicating a node would\n"
      "be content creation, which D2 puts out of scope for this editor.\n"
      "\n"
      "CORRECTION to 'delete'. D3 is explicit: Delete and Backspace remove\n"
      "annotations, and hiding a node is a separate command that is never\n"
      "bound to Delete. The shipped implementation hides every selected node,\n"
      "so Delete currently makes nodes disappear from a graph the editor is\n"
      "not allowed to edit. After this pillar 'delete' removes selected\n"
      "annotations and does nothing to nodes, edges or groups.\n"
      "\n"
      "The hide-nodes behaviour is NOT dropped. It moves to its own 'hide'\n"
      "command, present in this registry and bound to no chord in KEYMAP.\n"
      "The Delete command is the only path to setNodesHiddenEdit in the whole\n"
      "editor today, so removing hiding from Delete without putting it\n"
      "somewhere would leave no way to hide a node from any surface until\n"
      "editor-shell ships a menu -- a regression window for a feature that\n"
      "currently works. Unbound-but-present costs one registry entry and\n"
      "closes it.\n"
      "\n"
      "§6 also asks for a status hint when Delete is pressed on a\n"
      "non-annotation. There is no surface for a hint until the editor-shell\n"
      "status island exists, so Delete on a node is silent for now."
    type: { unsupported: { reason: RAW_EXPRESSION, source_excerpt: "Array<Command>" } }
    uses: ["Command", "CommandContext", "deleteAnnotationEdit", "duplicateAnnotationEdit", "addAnnotationEdit", "setNodesHiddenEdit", "newAnnotationId", "NEW_ANNOTATION_TEXT", "clearSelection", "elementKey"]
  }
]
